{"content":[{"c":["MERAIOTH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Levite, six to seven generations removed from Aaron (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.6-7","r":"1Chr.6.6-7","rawR":"1Chr.6.6-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.6-7","value":"1Chr.6.6-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:6-7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.7.3","r":"Ezra.7.3","rawR":"Ezra.7.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.7.3","value":"Ezra.7.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 7:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Ahitub’s son and the father of Zadok (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.11","r":"1Chr.9.11","rawR":"1Chr.9.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.11","value":"1Chr.9.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.11","r":"Neh.11.11","rawR":"Neh.11.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.11","value":"Neh.11.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:11"},"); perhaps identifiable with #1 above, despite differences in genealogy."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Priestly house whose head was Helkai during the days of Joiakim in postexilic Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.15","r":"Neh.12.15","rawR":"Neh.12.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.15","value":"Neh.12.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:15"},"). Its forebear is given as Meremoth (v ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.3","r":"Neh.12.3","rawR":"Neh.12.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.3","value":"Neh.12.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"3"},"). Some regard ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.15","r":"Neh.12.15","rawR":"Neh.12.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.15","value":"Neh.12.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nehemiah 12:15"}," as a scribal error and identify the names in verses ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.3","r":"Neh.12.3","rawR":"Neh.12.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.3","value":"Neh.12.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"3"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.15","r":"Neh.12.15","rawR":"Neh.12.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.15","value":"Neh.12.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"15"}," as the same person."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Meraioth","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6